- How would you test this workflow end-to-end?
- How would you audit changes made during containment?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess hands-on orchestration across Azure components during incidents, focusing on tenant isolation, automated rollback safety, and auditable controls.

## Key Concepts
- UEBA-driven automation (Defender for Cloud/Sentinel)
- Per-tenant network isolation (NSG, Private Endpoint)
- Key Vault key rotation and re-encryption
- Token revocation and Conditional Access control
- Canary-based rollback mechanisms
- Centralized auditing and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator snippet
async function quarantineTenant(tenantId){
  await applyPerTenantNSG(tenantId);
  await rotateKeyVaultKeys(tenantId);
  await revokeTokensAndDisableCA(tenantId);
  await rollbackToLastGoodRelease(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region data governance with fine-grained access control, dynamic masking, and comprehensive auditability using Azure Purview, Synapse RBAC, Conditional Access, and Privileged Identity Management.

## Key Concepts
- Data classification and lineage tracking with Azure Purview
- Fine-grained access control in Synapse and ADLS Gen2
- Dynamic data masking with query-time enforcement
- Privileged Identity Management and Conditional Access integration
- End-to-end rollout, rollback, and testing methodologies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo example: determine if masking is required for a query
function requiresMasking(userId, dataset, column) {
  // Check Purview classification and user permissions
  const classification = purview.getClassification(dataset, column);
  const userAccess = synapseRBAC.checkPermissions(userId, dataset);

  // Apply masking based on sensitivity and user role
  return classification.sensitivity === 'High' && 
         !userAccess.hasColumnLevelAccess;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic network security controls in Azure and practical rollout/rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Private Link and Private Endpoints
- Storage Account network rules (default deny)
- Azure Policy enforcement
- Rollback and test strategies

## Code Example
```bicep
param storageAccountName string
param vnetSubnetId string
resource pe 'Microsoft.Network/privateEndpoints@2020-11-01' = {
  name: '${storageAccountName}-pe'
  location: resourceGroup().location
  properties: {
    subnet: { id: vnetSubnetId }
    privateLinkServiceConnections: [
      {
        name: 'storageBlob'
        properties: {
          privateLinkServiceId: '/subscriptions/.../resourceGroups/.../providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/${storageAccountName}'
          groupIds: [ 'blob' ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "not": { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/privateEndpointConnections", "exists": true } }
        }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

